# Session 2 Assignments – JavaScript Objects & References

## Overview
This session focuses on **JavaScript Objects**, **Object Operations**, and **Reference Handling**, which are important concepts in writing structured and reusable JavaScript code.

These assignments help in understanding how JavaScript stores data, manipulates object properties, and works with reference types.

---

##  Topics Covered
- JavaScript Objects
- Object Properties
- Object Manipulation
- Reference Variables
- Data Handling
- Logical Operations
- JavaScript Fundamentals

---

##  Assignments Included

### 1. Amount Using Reference
**File:** `Amout_using_Reference.js`  
- Demonstrates how reference variables work in JavaScript  
- Shows data storage and value manipulation using object references  
- Helps understand memory/reference concepts

### 2. Objects and Object Operations
**File:** `Objects_and_Obj_Operations.js`  
- Creating objects in JavaScript  
- Adding new properties  
- Updating object values  
- Deleting properties  
- Accessing object data using dot notation / bracket notation

---

##  Technologies Used
- JavaScript (ES6)
- Node.js
- VS Code
- Git & GitHub

